From 231ea20cf247156c043934552dc9292b3e817255 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NBG-TOPGEE <NBG-TOPGEE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 00:45:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Integrate authentication with Spring Boot backend

- Unwrap the backend's {success,data,message,code} envelope in the
  Axios client and normalize errors into a small ApiError shape.
- Rewrite src/api/auth.ts to match the real Spring Boot DTOs
  (RegisterRequest/LoginRequest/User) and map the backend's user
  shape (numeric id, upper-case role) to the frontend User type.
  Removed the call to a nonexistent /auth/logout endpoint - the
  backend is stateless JWT with no server-side logout route.
- useAuth now validates a persisted session against GET /auth/me on
  load and signs out cleanly on an invalid/expired token, while
  keeping the same public interface so Navbar/checkout/__root are
  unchanged.
- Implemented the /login and /register pages (previously stubs),
  wired to the real backend and matching the existing design system.

No other files touched. tsc --noEmit and npm run build both pass;
the one remaining tsc error (orders.local.ts) is pre-existing on
main and unrelated to this change.
